0:00:00.000,0:00:15.000
Welcome to this extended presentation about the history of computing and its impact on modern society. We will cover many topics in detail.

0:00:15.000,0:00:30.000
In the early days, computers were massive machines that filled entire rooms. They used vacuum tubes and punch cards for input and output operations.

0:00:30.000,0:00:45.000
The invention of the transistor revolutionized everything. Suddenly, computers could be made smaller, faster, and more reliable than ever before imagined.

0:00:45.000,0:01:00.000
Then came the integrated circuit, which allowed thousands of transistors to be placed on a single chip. This was the beginning of the microprocessor era.

0:01:00.000,0:01:15.000
The personal computer revolution of the 1980s brought computing into homes and offices around the world, changing how people work and communicate forever.

0:01:15.000,0:01:30.000
The internet connected these personal computers globally, creating a network of information that has transformed every aspect of human civilization profoundly.
